animated by writing the hebrew word "Emet" on the golems forehead.
"Emet" (or is it "Emeth" ?) is hebrew and means "Thuth" or "God".

the most famous golem was the one created by the rabbi Jehudah Ben Bezalel
in the 15th century in Prag.

When the Golem turned 'bad', the rabbi erased the letter E from the golems
forehead. making the writing to be "met" that is the hebrew word for "Dead"
and the golem was destroyed.

